   "subject": "Re: SpectronauttoMSstatsFormat",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>these are Spectronaut&#39;s quality scores at different levels (pg = protein group etc). <br></div><div>NA means we treat the values as missing randomly at the imputation step, 0 means missing due to low intensity.</div><div>Missing values treatment is described here: <a href=\"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jproteome.2c00834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jproteome.2c00834&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793230716027000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DR21pmU0lbTAkxqV3bxm-\">https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jproteome.2c00834</a></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Kind regards,</div><div>Mateusz <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">środa, 7 lutego 2024 o 12:53:36 UTC+1 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">suniya....@gmail.com</a> napisał(a):<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Dear MSstats team, <div><br></div><div>I am new to MSstats and are trying to understand how the different functions work. I would like to understand the following steps that is performed during Spectronaut file conversion using SpectronauttoMSstatsFormat in MSstats version 4. </div><div><br></div><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">INFO \r\n[2024-01-23 12:04:46] ** Intensities with values not smaller than 0.01\r\nin PGQvalue are replaced with NA</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:1pt none windowtext;padding:0cm\">INFO \r\n[2024-01-23 12:04:46] ** Intensities with values not smaller than 0.01\r\nin EGQvalue are replaced with 0</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\">What is being filtered here?</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\">Kind regards</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\">Suniya</p></div></blockquote></div>"
